# Environment Variables — PortFlow AI

This file documents all environment variables used across the PortFlow AI
application. Component-specific `.env.example` files are the authoritative
reference for each service.

## Backend (src/backend/.env.example)

| Variable          | Purpose                             | Development value                                          |
|-------------------|-------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------|
| APP_NAME          | API display name                    | PortFlow AI API                                            |
| APP_ENV           | Runtime environment                 | development                                                |
| API_V1_PREFIX     | API route prefix                    | /api/v1                                                    |
| DATABASE_URL      | PostgreSQL connection string        | postgresql+psycopg://portflow:portflow@localhost:5432/portflow |
| CORS_ORIGINS      | Allowed browser origins (JSON list) | ["http://localhost:5173"]                                  |
| LOG_LEVEL         | Application log level               | INFO                                                       |

## Frontend (src/frontend/.env.example)

| Variable               | Purpose                          |
|------------------------|----------------------------------|
| VITE_API_BASE_URL      | Base URL for REST API calls      |
| VITE_DEFAULT_PORT_ID   | Optional default terminal ID     |

## Rules

- Never commit a real `.env` file — it is in `.gitignore`.
- Copy the example files before starting:
  ```powershell
  Copy-Item src\backend\.env.example src\backend\.env
  Copy-Item src\frontend\.env.example src\frontend\.env
  ```
- IBM Cloud and external API keys (if added later) must also go in `.env`,
  never in committed files or source code.
